{"name":"Silence Is Golden","hex":"#c2a06d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silence is golden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proverb","definitions":["Peace and quiet have great value.","Often the best choice is to say nothing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silence_is_golden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silence Is Golden (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Silence Is Golden\" is a song initially recorded by the American rock band the Four Seasons. Written by Bob Crewe and Bob Gaudio, Philips Records released it in 1964 as the B-side of the U.S. number 1 single \"Rag Doll\", which was also written by Crewe and Gaudio. The Tremeloes' 1967 cover version reached number 1 on the UK Singles Chart and number 11 on the US charts."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silence_Is_Golden_(song)","wikidata":"Q2742283"},{"title":"Silence Is Golden (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Silence Is Golden is a 15-minute award-winning film written and directed by Chris Shepherd and produced by Maria Manton. Set in 1970s Britain, it tells the story of a 10-year-old boy's obsession with his seemingly simple-minded neighbour Dennis. The film mixes live action with various form of animation, including stop frame, drawn 2D. The complex mixture of styles enables Shepherd to show Billy's fantasies and inner thoughts on screen."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silence_Is_Golden_(film)","wikidata":"Q12127503"},{"title":"Silence","blocks":[{"text":"Silence is the absence of ambient audible sound, the emission of sounds of such low intensity that they do not draw attention to themselves, or the state of having ceased to produce sounds; this latter sense can be extended to apply to the cessation or absence of any form of communication, whether through speech or other medium. Remaining mute can be a symptom of mental illness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg/330px-Faras_Saint_Anne_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silence","wikidata":"Q502261"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/SilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg/250px-SilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/SilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/18/SilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg/250px-SilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilenceIsGoldenTremeloes.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/500px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/1280px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg/500px-Geraasvrye_gebied%2C_Manie_van_der_Schijff_BT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Keep silent sign in South Africa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeraasvrye_gebie